      },
      "message": "affordance: fixed-order class summary in diff output (apify#1514 lesson)\n\nThe campaign once retold a prose-only window as 'silent breaking change'\nin public (apify#1514, retracted): the grader was right on both ends of\nthe timeline, the human retelling was not - per-line classes were\ncorrect but there was no headline count, and the eye caught 'DRIFT\nDETECTED'. Two affordance fixes, per the research chat's handoff:\n\n- summarizeVerdicts(report) in pins.js: one line, fixed order\n  (breaking / loosened / expanded / mirrored / notation / cosmetic /\n  annotation / identity / policy / prompt / resource / new / gone),\n  unknown future classes appended and never hidden. Zeroes are stated,\n  not implied by absence.\n- CLI: 'rugsnare diff summary: ...' printed to stderr in EVERY mode\n  (incl. --json/--sarif - diagnostics never corrupt the data stream),\n  on both the normal path and the POLICY stop path. This is the citable\n  'what did the grader actually say' line for the campaign rule\n  'no label without a grader'.\n- PR-comment renderer: the same summary is the FIRST content line of\n  the comment body (and of the POLICY body), before any per-tool\n  section - a prose-only window can no longer be retold as breaking by\n  someone skimming the comment.\n\nTests 394 -> 395 (unit: counts + unknown class + clean-store zeros;\ne2e: prose-only drift asserts the full zero-breaking summary line).",
      "tree": {
